    "https://about.colum.edu/provost/faculty-senate.html": {
      "title": "Faculty Senate",
      "description": "Faculty Senate - Columbia College Chicago Skip to main content Academics Schools Audio and Music Business and Entrepreneurship Communication and Culture Design Fashion Film and Television Theatre and Dance Visual Arts Programs Majors Minors Graduate Certificate Pre-College Programs Immersive Studies Study Abroad Semester in LA Comedy Studies Academic Resources Academic Advising Academic Calendar Catalog Experential Learning Library Our Faculty Student Tools MyColumbia Portal Canvas Engage IT Assistance Student Hub Admissions + Financial Aid Why Choose Columbia? Chicago: Our City and Campus World-Class Facilities Faculty Mentors and Makers Industry Connections Alumni Success Student Work How to Apply Freshman Transfer Graduate International Second Bachelor's Returning Students Nondegree Seeking Portfolio and Audition Requirements Cost + Aid Financial Aid Scholarships Tuition and Fees Admitted Students Undergraduate Graduate Orientation Visit Us Campus Visits Virtual Tours Student Experience Campus Life Student Center Student Organizations Athletics and Recreation Student Spotlights Events on Campus Manifest Arts Festival Housing + Living Campus Housing Options Office of Housing and Residential Experience Living in Chicago Campus Facilities Campus Map Services + Support Campus Safety and Security Student Health Support Services MyColumbia Portal Information Technology Student Handbook Student Success Student Financial Services Academic Advising Belonging and Persistence Holistic Support Career Outcomes Career Advising Alumni Success Rankings and Awards About About the College Facts Mission and History Rankings and Awards Academic Access and Excellence Strategic Plan Contact Us Leadership Office of the President Office of the Provost Board of Trustees News + Events Columbia Stories Media Mentions Event Spotlight 135th Anniversary Media Resources Careers + Alumni Career Center Internships Job Board Industry Partnerships Alumni Success The Alumni Network Get Info Apply Visit Give Search colum.edu Quick Links MyColumbia Canvas Library Academic Calendar Commencement Campus Map Building Hours Resources For Current Students Prospective Students Parents and Families Student Counselors and Advocates Faculty and Staff Alumni Donors Employers Health + Safety Campus Safety and Security Health Services Center for Student Wellbeing Services for Students with Disabilities Report a Concern Get Connected Give to Columbia Work at Columbia Hire from Columbia Directory Contact Us Get Info Apply Visit Give Search and quick links Open navigation menu Office of the Provost Academic Leadership Academic Personnel Academic Policies and Resources Accreditation and Assessment Columbia Core Curriculum Academic Access and Excellence Emeriti Faculty Members Faculty Careers Faculty Development Portfolio Faculty Senate Global Education Institutional Review Board Office of the Registrar Transfer Initiatives and Academic Partnerships About Columbia Office of the Provost Faculty Senate Faculty Senate The Columbia College Chicago Faculty Senate is an officially sanctioned body within the governance structure of the College. The Senate embodies the principles of shared governance and is driven by the collective will, expertise, and creative energy of its full-time faculty. The Senate empowers the faculty to provide authoritative communication and collaboration with the president of the College, chief academic officers, and others regarding policies and practices pertaining to academic excellence, creative and scholarly endeavors, and professional responsibility and conditions of employment. The Senate is the principle body responsible for deliberations, formulations and recommendations concerning academic policy at the College. Senators Michael Brown , Theatre and Dance David Castellanos , Theatre and Dance Cheri Charlton , Visual Arts Robert Edgecomb , Film and Television Betsy Edgerton , Communication and Culture Ron Fleischer , Film and Television David Gerding , Film and Television Visda Goudarzi , Audio and Music Julie Granata-Hunicutt , Theatre and Dance Jason Hopkins , Film and Television Rene King , Design Dawn Larsen , Business and Entrepreneurship Elio Leturia , Communication and Culture Teerath Majumber , Audio and Music Peg Murphy , Business and Entrepreneurship Michael Pogue , Theatre and Dance Brendan Riley , Communication and Culture Lee Sanders , Audio and Music K. Crom Saunders , Communication and Culture Jackie Spinner , Communication and Culture Kendra Thulin , Theatre and Dance Ayo Walker , Theatre and Dance Rick Walker , Theatre and Dance Goji Young , Fashion Standing Committees Executive The Executive Committee sets the agenda for each senate meeting, manages senate business, communicates with internal and external stakeholders, and actively pursues the implementation of senate recommendations.​​ David Gerding , President Dawn Larsen , Vice President Brendan Riley , Secretary Betsy Edgerton Peg Murphy Academic Affairs The Academic Affairs Committee considers issues relevant to graduate and undergraduate, in-person, hybrid, and online teaching and learning at Columbia College Chicago.​ Julie Granata-Hunicutt , Vice Chair Kendra Thulin , Vice Chair K. Crom Saunders , Secretary Ron Fleischer Eilo Leturia Cheri Charlton Faculty Affairs The Faculty Affairs Committee considers issues that impact workplace conditions for faculty at Columbia College Chicago. Robert Edgecomb Rene King Micheel Pogue Jackie Spinner Ayo Walker Ric Walker Goli Young Financial Affairs The Financial Affairs Committee collaborates with the administration on fiscal matters that impact teaching, learning, and faculty affairs. Lee Sanders , Vice Chair Jason Hopkins , Secretary Michael Brown David Castellanos Visda Goudarzi Teerath Majumber Bylaws and Responsibilities The Senate Bylaws were written and approved by the faculty Spring 2011. They were approved by the Columbia College Board of Trustees on October 6, 2012. Faculty Senate Bylaws Senator Responsibilities​ The Columbia College Faculty Senate empowers “the faculty to exercise leadership and apply their expertise towards” the overall health and effectiveness of the institution (Bylaws 2.3.3). Rather than wielding power as individual members of the Senate, Senators work collectively as a representative body to leverage the expertise of faculty for purposes of shared decision-making and leadership. To this end, consulting regularly with faculty constituents and representing the collective will of these stakeholders—at standing committee and full Senate meetings—is critical to maintaining the Senate’s position as “a mechanism by which the faculty can authoritatively communicate with the administration and constituencies both within and beyond Columbia College Chicago” (2.3.2). The following summaries of Department/School Senator responsibilities are meant to provide general guidelines for the expectations associated with the Senator role: Department Senator Responsibilities Represent the collective will, expertise and authority of the faculty within your department regarding matters pertaining to teaching, learning and faculty life.* Include a summary of Senate business at regular departmental meetings Solicit input from faculty about Senate matters, especially those requiring an upcoming vote, in an effort to truly represent the voice of your department Remind faculty of upcoming Senate meetings and invite them to attend The above can be conducted via e-mail and in standing faculty meetings Attend all Senate meetings Attend all standing committee meetings School Senator Responsibilities Represent the collective will, expertise and authority of the faculty within your school regarding matters pertaining to school-wide concerns.* Attend all Senate meetings Attend all standing committee meetings Introduce themselves as School-wide representatives at school-wide faculty and briefly update their colleagues on College or School-wide issues under review by the Faculty Senate Standing Committee Chairperson Responsibilities Schedule, create agenda, and document minutes for monthly meetings. Submit minutes via email to the Secretary of the Executive Committee Meet with the Executive Committee on an as-needed basis to receive charges and discuss progress Prepare a report of committee, subcommittee, and workgroup business and orally present at all scheduled Faculty Senate meetings Prepare an annual written report summarizing work completed, outstanding actionable items, and future business, including the work of any subcommittees and workgroups, to be submitted via email to the Secretary of the Executive Committee by the final Faculty Senate meeting of the academic year Establish sub committees or workgroups after a majority vote of those senators in attendance at the meeting such is proposed Issue the subcommittee or workgroup a specific charge, a membership roster, and a project timeline *Adapted from Faculty Senate Bylaws, 2.1, emphasis added For additional infomation, including agendas and minutes, visit the Intranet Faculty Senate site . Office of the Provost Academic Leadership Academic Personnel Academic Policies and Resources Accreditation and Assessment Columbia Core Curriculum Academic Access and Excellence Emeriti Faculty Members Faculty Careers Faculty Development Portfolio Faculty Senate Global Education Institutional Review Board Office of the Registrar Transfer Initiatives and Academic Partnerships Columbia College Chicago homepage Columbia College Chicago Instagram Columbia College Chicago Facebook Columbia College Chicago LinkedIn Columbia College Chicago YouTube Academics Admissions + Financial Aid Student Experience About Careers & Alumni INFO FOR Students Faculty and Staff Parents Alumni Contact Us Academics Schools Majors & Programs Academic Calendar Our Faculty Request Info Admissions + Financial Aid Application Requirements Portfolios and Auditions Financial Aid Scholarships 